# Nesting demonstration

This section is a **living example** of how the GOV.UK Tech Docs Template builds a multi-level sidebar from nested folders. It is not product documentation — use it to try the left-hand navigation and to copy the folder pattern when adding deeper sections.

`multipage_nav` and `collapsible_nav` are already enabled in `config/tech-docs.yml`. Nesting comes from directories under `design_docs/source/`, each containing an `index.html.md.erb` with a `weight` in the frontmatter.

## How this tree is laid out on disk

```text
design_docs/source/nesting-demo/
├── index.html.md.erb                 ← this page (weight 80)
├── first-level/
│   ├── index.html.md.erb             ← weight 81
│   └── second-level/
│       ├── index.html.md.erb         ← weight 82
│       └── third-level/
│           └── index.html.md.erb     ← weight 83
└── sibling-branch/
    └── index.html.md.erb             ← weight 84
```

## Rules of thumb

- One folder = one page in the sidebar; put content in that folder’s `index.html.md.erb`.
- Nested folders become nested nav items (with collapsible expand/collapse when `collapsible_nav` is on).
- Lower `weight` values appear higher; “heavier pages sink to the bottom”.
- Child weights must sit between their parent and the next sibling at the parent’s level so order stays coherent.

